+
+# Edit and verify a calculation
+
+Understand saved calculations and completeness checks. Run operations on your {term}`modelo`. Read how-to guides for step-by-step actions.
+
+## Treat a calculation as a saved version
+
+Save the result each time you run a calculation. Do not overwrite previous versions. Keep earlier versions on disk.
+
+Treat every calculation as a distinct saved version. Compare versions. Go back to previous versions. Wait to commit numbers until you decide they are final.
+
+## Edit and recalculate
+
+Import bank data for some numbers. Enter missing figures by hand. Correct calculated values. Recalculate to produce a new saved version.
+
+Give each required casilla a value. Recalculate to update totals. See [Review and supply calculation inputs](../how-to/review-calculation-values.md) for detailed steps.
+
+## Verify a calculation
+
+Run a completeness check over a draft. Verify three conditions:
+
+- Supply a value for every required box.
+- Make sums add up consistently.
+- Resolve any blocking issues.
+
+Read the published rules for the modelo and year. Measure your draft against the rules. Save the verification report.
+
+## Review verification states
+
+Check the draft state after verification:
+
+- **Complete.** Pass the completeness check. Keep the version in a locked state.
+- **Incomplete.** Fill required boxes. Re-run the check.
+- **Blocked.** Resolve failed rules or consistency problems. Re-run the check.
+
+Read the saved report. Identify empty required boxes. Find failed rules. Separate blocking issues from warnings. Read [understand a verification report](../how-to/verification-reports.md) for instructions.
+
+## Understand verification limits
+
+Treat a passed check as a local confirmation of consistency. Do not assume the following:
+
+- **Agency acceptance.** Do not assume AEAT accepts your filing. The tool does not contact AEAT.
+- **Upload guarantee.** Do not assume submission to AEAT will succeed. Submit the form separately.
+- **Deadline compliance.** Do not assume you are on time. The check ignores filing deadlines.
+
+Treat a passed check only as "my draft is complete and consistent".
+
+## Require a verified version for upload
+
+Verify a version before you build the upload file. Do not use an unverified draft.
+
+Protect your filing process. Use the completeness check to prevent accidental submission of incomplete drafts.
+
+## Navigate the pipeline
+
+Read the [Understanding the AEAT pipeline](index.md) cluster. See [How filings build on earlier ones](building-on-earlier-filings.md) to carry forward a verified prior period. Go to [Reviewing your numbers and producing the upload file](reviewing-and-exporting.md) to review results and create the upload file.
